# Cursor Cloud adapter

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for Nebula identity, authority, state safety, secrets, Git, and verification. This file adds only Cursor Cloud navigation and host checks.

- Inspect the current host's Node and `vp` availability against `package.json`; do not assume a particular VM image, login-shell PATH, SDK installation, or port.
- For web launch, authenticated pairing, isolated state, and retained environments, use [test-t3-app](../../.agents/skills/test-t3-app/SKILL.md). Browser `dev`/`dev:web` is single-origin; desktop has a separate origin configuration.
- For Android or iOS, use [test-t3-mobile](../../.agents/skills/test-t3-mobile/SKILL.md). Check SDK/device availability before choosing a build path. An unavailable emulator is a host limitation, not proof of an app defect.
- Check current patches and toolchain evidence before treating an old native failure as a blocker. A resolved patch defect does not prove full Android health; validate the affected native path when needed.
- Verify only changed scope. Do not run a repo-wide formatter or grant permanent flaky-test exemptions from old setup observations. Report reproducible failures with revision, command, and evidence in the relevant issue.
